<h3>ASP.NET Core Data Protection</h3>
<ul>
    <li>Application name <code>ForestChurches-App</code>, so every instance shares one key ring.</li>
    <li>Production: key ring XML persisted to Azure Blob Storage (<code>blob-container-name</code> / <code>blob-file-name</code>) and each key encrypted ("wrapped") with the Key Vault key in <code>data-key</code>. If the Key Vault protector can't be configured, the app logs a warning and keeps the ring in blob storage <strong>unwrapped</strong>.</li>
    <li>Development: keys in the local <code>DataProtectionKeys</code> folder (unencrypted).</li>
    <li>A new key is created every 7 days; old keys stay available to decrypt older data until they expire (default retention).</li>
    <li>Payloads are encrypted with AES-256-CBC and authenticated with HMAC-SHA256 (Data Protection defaults).</li>
</ul>
<p>Losing or replacing the key ring signs everyone out and breaks every outstanding email link and protected ID. Don't delete the blob or disable old versions of <code>data-key</code>.</p>

<h3>Encryption summary</h3>
<div class="docs-table-wrap">
    <table class="docs-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Data</th><th>In transit</th><th>At rest</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td>Browser ↔ website</td><td>TLS (HTTPS, HSTS)</td><td>–</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Website ↔ email app</td><td>TLS, JWT</td><td>Email content held in the email app's memory until sent.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Email app ↔ IONOS</td><td>STARTTLS when available (not enforced)</td><td>IONOS mailbox.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Website ↔ database</td><td>Depends on <code>SslMode</code> in the connection string (check it's <code>Required</code> or stricter)</td><td>Depends on the database host's disk encryption.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Passwords</td><td>–</td><td>PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512 hash.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Authenticator keys, recovery codes</td><td>–</td><td><strong>Plain text</strong> in <code>AspNetUserTokens</code> (Identity default).</td></tr>
            <tr><td>ChurchSuite access/refresh tokens</td><td>–</td><td><strong>Plain text</strong> in <code>ChurchSuiteCredentials</code>.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Images, key ring (blob)</td><td>TLS</td><td>Azure Storage service-side encryption (on by default); key ring additionally wrapped by Key Vault.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Secrets</td><td>TLS</td><td>Key Vault (HSM-backed encryption).</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Logs</td><td>TLS to Grafana; database as above</td><td>Plain text in <code>applicationlogs</code> and Grafana Cloud.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

